If i assemble a stone golem and include a stone carving of a brain
within it, then animate the assemblage, then the golem has a brain; one
that serves no purpose, however. With my sense of humor, i'd probably
have put the brain where its bottom belongs. :)

Or (even sillier), the golem has been rampaging around the dungeon,
killing things, and taking the brain from each monster as a trophy.
Therefore "The mind flayer eats the golem's brain" means it grabbed at
the decaying corpse the golem was carrying. "The golem doesn't notice"
means it wasn't paying attention...



